# GTKX Code Examples

## App Structure

### Minimal App

```tsx
// src/index.tsx
import { applicationId } from "@gtkx/config/runtime";
import { GtkApplication, GtkApplicationWindow, GtkLabel } from "@gtkx/jsx/gtk";
import { render, quit } from "@gtkx/react";

const App = () => (
    <GtkApplication applicationId={applicationId}>
        <GtkApplicationWindow
            title="Hello"
            defaultWidth={400}
            defaultHeight={300}
            onCloseRequest={() => {
                quit();
                return true;
            }}
        >
            <GtkLabel label="Hello, World!" />
        </GtkApplicationWindow>
    </GtkApplication>
);

render(<App />);
```

The entry calls `render` directly (similar to `createRoot().render()` in `react-dom`). The `<GtkApplication>` component constructs, registers, and activates the GTK application; pass its `applicationId` explicitly, reading the one declared in `gtkx.config.ts` from `@gtkx/config/runtime`. `gtkx dev` restarts the Node process on entry-level changes so the top-level call only runs once per process life.

### Modern Adwaita App

```tsx
import { applicationId } from "@gtkx/config/runtime";
import * as Gtk from "@gtkx/gi/gtk";
import { AdwApplication, AdwApplicationWindow, AdwHeaderBar, AdwToolbarView, AdwWindowTitle, AdwStatusPage } from "@gtkx/jsx/adw";
import { quit } from "@gtkx/react";
import { GtkButton } from "@gtkx/jsx/gtk";

const MainWindow = () => (
    <AdwApplicationWindow
        title="My App"
        defaultWidth={800}
        defaultHeight={600}
        onCloseRequest={() => {
            quit();
            return true;
        }}
    >
        <AdwToolbarView
            addTopBar={
                <AdwHeaderBar titleWidget={<AdwWindowTitle title="My App" subtitle="Welcome" />} />
            }
        >
            <AdwStatusPage
                iconName="applications-system-symbolic"
                title="Welcome"
                description="Get started with your GTKX app"
                vexpand
            >
                <GtkButton label="Get Started" cssClasses={["suggested-action", "pill"]} halign={Gtk.Align.CENTER} />
            </AdwStatusPage>
        </AdwToolbarView>
    </AdwApplicationWindow>
);

export const App = () => (
    <AdwApplication applicationId={applicationId}>
        <MainWindow />
    </AdwApplication>
);
```

